//      run once per ladder level, per setup, per book, on every confirmed bar. That was
//      the hottest loop in the file and it grew with the pool. SdLadder now carries an
//      `hits` bool array index-parallel with `lines`, so the test is one .get(). The
//      registry and its 300/100 drain are gone.
//      It also closes a latent hazard: sdHitLns held refs to lines that f_clearLadder had
//      already deleted, and read prices off them. A latch that lives INSIDE the ladder
//      dies with the ladder, so a culled setup can no longer leave a stale ref behind.
//      Same pattern MM IFVG has used since its v6.0 (iH1-iH4). Both files, one mechanism.
//   2) pcDirs DELETED. The CISD FVG layer pushed a direction column that nothing ever
//      read. It was redundant twice over: slot already encodes direction (bSlot = who*2,
//      sSlot = who*2+1, so even = bull, odd = bear) and pcOwner already stores slot. The
//      `dir` parameter came off f_pcAdd with it - it fed nothing else.
//   3) f_lqSize() -> f_szName(string). Same output, but MM IFVG calls the identical
//      mapper f_szName and passes the input in. One name, one shape, one place to fix.
// v4.43
// v4.43: RENAMED TO "CISD FVG". Ryan's call, taken before it reaches a guide or the site and
